<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moussa ag Amastan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1867–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moussa ag Amastan was amenokal, or paramount chief, of the Kel Ahaggar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> from 1905 until his death in 1920. After French forces defeated the Tuareg at Tit in 1902 he submitted to French rule and became a close friend of the hermit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-foucauld">Charles de Foucauld</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamanrasset">Tamanrasset</a>. He kept the Kel Ahaggar out of the Senussi-led Tuareg revolt of 1916–1917.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moussa-ag-amastan.jpg" alt="Moussa ag Amastan" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown Public domainPublic domainfalsefalse This work is in the public domain in its country of origin and other cou... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MousaAgAmastane-Paris.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
